      "text": "To solve the expression \\(1 - 4 + 7 - 10 + 13 - \\cdots - 46 + 49 - 52 + 55\\), we first identify the pattern in the sequence. The sequence alternates between adding positive and subtracting negative numbers, which corresponds to the coefficients in the arithmetic sequence 1, 4, 7, 10, ..., 55, 52.\n\nFirst, we determine the number of terms in the sequence. The general term of the sequence is \\(3k - 2\\), where \\(k\\) is a positive integer. We need to find the value of \\(k\\) such that \\(3k - 2 = 55\\):\n\\[\n3k - 2 = 55 \\implies 3k = 57 \\implies k = 19.\n\\]\nSo, there are 19 terms in the sequence. The sum of the sequence can be calculated by summing the positive terms and subtracting the sum of the negative terms.\n\nThe positive terms form an arithmetic sequence with the first term \\(a = 1\\), the common difference \\(d = 3\\), and the number of terms \\(n = 19\\). The sum of the first \\(n\\) terms of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n\\[\nS_n = \\frac{n}{2} (2a + (n-1)d).\n\\]\nSubstituting the values, we get:\n\\[\nS_{19} = \\frac{19}{2} (2 \\cdot 1 + (19-1) \\cdot 3) = \\frac{19}{2} (2 + 18 \\cdot 3) = \\frac{19}{2} (2 + 54) = \\frac{19}{2} \\cdot 56 = 19 \\cdot 28 = 532.\n\\]\nThe negative terms form an arithmetic sequence with the first term \\(a = -4\\), the common difference \\(d = -3\\), and the number of terms \\(n = 19\\). The sum of the first \\(n\\) terms of this arithmetic sequence is given by:\n\\[\nS_n = \\frac{n}{2} (2a + (n-1)d).\n\\]\nSubstituting the values, we get:\n\\[\nS_{19} = \\frac{19}{2} (2 \\cdot -4 + (19-1) \\cdot -3) = \\frac{19}{2} (-8 + 18 \\cdot -3) = \\frac{19}{2} (-8 - 54) = \\frac{19}{2} \\cdot -62 = 19 \\cdot -31 = -589.\n\\]\nThe total sum of the expression is the sum of the positive terms minus the sum of the negative terms:\n\\[\n532 - (-589) = 532 + 589 = 1121.\n\\]\nThus, the value of the expression is \\(\\boxed{1121}\\).",
